storyScenes.opening:
I've found the two sentences again. One's from the first look. One's from the return.

{two-looks}

I've put them where they can see each other. They're on facing leaves, with the gutter between them, the way two people sit across a table. If the thing stayed the same, then I've got two looks at the same thing, and that's worth keeping on its own. I won't scribble a miracle where there was none.

